#: packs/official/firefox/README.md
msgid "Firefox privacy"
msgstr ""

#: packs/official/firefox/README.md
msgid ""
"Makes Firefox harder for websites to track you: it turns on Firefox's strongest anti-fingerprinting (`resistFingerprinting`, from Tor Browser), with letterboxing, WebRTC limits, strict tracking protection, HTTPS-only mode and daily re-randomized canvas readings."
msgstr ""

#: packs/official/firefox/README.md
msgid ""
"Makes Firefox harder for websites to track: strong anti-fingerprinting, letterboxing and WebRTC limits"
msgstr ""

#: packs/official/firefox/README.md
msgid ""
"The Frame's hardware (Adreno GPU, the VR desktop's unusual window sizes, touch input) is rare among browsers, so it's easy to fingerprint."
msgstr ""

#: packs/official/float-grab/README.md
msgid ""
"\"Float in World\" also picks the window up for placing, like grabbing its bar; your next click (or letting go of the trigger) puts it down"
msgstr ""

#: packs/official/float-grab/README.md
msgid ""
"\"Float in World\" also picks the window up, as grabbing the bar under it does, so you place it in one go; your next click (or letting go of the trigger, if you're still holding it) puts it down."
msgstr ""

#: packs/official/float-grab/README.md
msgid ""
"In SteamVR, floating a window and then placing it takes two steps: press Float in World, then grab the bar under the window. This makes it one."
msgstr ""

#: packs/official/float-grab/README.md
msgid "Pick up when floating"
msgstr ""

